%%%%%%Hand 3
https://tinyurl.com/2369kszg
qx|A3|st||rh||ah|Board 3 IMPs   -   August 28, 2024|pn|hondo717,IraCT,danpsych,Sputniks|
md|1SK873HJ5DQT6CA976,SAT5HATDJ872CJ532,S642HK82D953CKT84,SQJ9HQ97643DAK4CQ|sv|e|
mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|mb|1H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|1@H is the correct opener here. However, in 4th seat you sometimes open 2@H. THAT IS NOT A WEAK 2. There is no point in opening a Weak-2 in 4th seat since you are not preempting the opponents. You can just pass. But there are hands where you should open 2@H or 2@S (or even 2@D) in 4th seat.|
PG| ***** 38 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at| Those are hands with a nice 6-card heart suit and a minimum opener (no more than 13 or a bad 14). East's hand does have 6 hearts, though the heart suit is not good enough and is a weak opener.|
PG| ***** 39 ***** |


mb|D|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I can now make a takeout double. It's a tad weak but okay since I passed originally. Had I not passed, I am not even close to a takeout double.|
PG| ***** 40 ***** |


mb|R|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I like redouble by West, showing 10+ HCP (10-12 here since West is a passed hand) 1N is also possible, but West is a bit strong for 1N.|
PG| ***** 41 ***** |


mb|P|mb|2H|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|East could have passed the redouble, but I like 2@H better. It makes it harder for us to compete and shows the 6th heart with a weak opening hand.|
PG| ***** 42 ***** |


mb|P|mb|?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|lb|*bBid for West.^^P|mb|P|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Pass by West is correct. He showed his 10 points and East did not make a game try.|
PG| ***** 44 ***** |


mb|P|
pg| ***** 45 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I have no good opening lead. Leading away from honors often gives away a trick. I don't like to lead unprotected aces (although that happens to work here). And leading a heart from Jx could easily give away a trick. So I have to decide whether to lead a spade or a diamond. A diamond is a bit more aggressive but could also give away a trick. So I will try a spade.|
PG| ***** 46 ***** |


