PG| ***** 86 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Good point. I should have bid 1@H. I was so excited about explaining |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=dummypoints,Bergen Dummy Points ^*N|CP||FP||at|, I forgot to look carefully at my hand.|
PG| ***** 87 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So let us keep 1@S here because I want to teach |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=dummypoints,Bergen Dummy Points ^*N|CP||FP||at|.|
PG| ***** 88 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|North's hand has 12 HCP, 2 length points, 1 quality suit point, and 4 points for the void (when you have a void the number of points you add is the number of trump you have) for 19 points. So North has a clear 3@S bid using Bergen Evaluation. A 3@S bid shows 17-19. This is a good example of where Bergen helps you evaluate hands much better than just using HCP and length.|
PG| ***** 89 ***** |


mb|3S|mb|P?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Had partner opened 1@C I have a clear 4@S bid. Technically, using |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=declarerpoints,Bergen Declarer Points^*N|CP||FP||at|, I have 6 HCP, 3 points for the void, and 2 points for the 2 outside 4-card suits which is 11, more than enough to bid 4@S.|
PG| ***** 90 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|But I don't like the diamond void given the 1@D opener. On the other hand, because this is IMPs and we are vulnerable, I will bid 4@S but not be surprised if we go down.|
PG| ***** 91 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In IMPs you stretch to bid games, especially when vulnerable and I would feel much better with a 5th spade, because 9 trumps is almost always worth one more trick than 8 trumps. |
PG| ***** 92 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In Match In match points I would not bid game because the advantage of making a close game is more than outweighed by the disadvantage that it will often go down.oints I would not bid game because the advantage of making a close game is more than outweighed by the disadvantage that it will often go down.|
PG| ***** 93 ***** |


