UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|It was so lucky to make it. It is a good example of how Bergen Hand Evaluation really helps you bid. I doubt whether many pairs, if any, would get to game. In fact most Norths would bid 2@S. But after my 1@S bid, North's hand, as you saw, becomes quite strong and Bergen Hand Evaluation helps you to figure that out. |
PG| ***** 109 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|That is why I recommend you go to my web site and look at my Bergen Hand Evaluation lessons. That is the single best way to improve your bidding. In fact, Kia is updating the Bergen Hand Evaluation movies. They will be appearing in my weekly email.|
PG| ***** 110 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Originally, had I bid 1@H and North bids 1 spade. After counting 9 or 10 |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=dummypoints,Bergen Dummy Points ^*N|CP||FP||at| I would bid 2@S.|
PG| ***** 111 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|If North invites, which she should (although 4@S by her would not be unreasonable, although she has the same issue with the heart void as I had with the diamond void). But if she bids 3@S, I would bid 4@S. So we still get there.|
PG| ***** 112 ***** |


